.DS_Store
node_modules
/build
/.svelte-kit
/package
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
vite.config.js.timestamp-*
vite.config.ts.timestamp-*

# Rust build output — 6+ GB, never belongs in the repo.
/src-tauri/target

# Local editor / tooling config.
/.claude
/.vscode

# Internal working notes. These name real people (debate partners and
# opponents), contain local Dropbox paths, and record session-by-session dev
# history. Kept out of the public repo on purpose.
/HANDOFF-*.md
/SESSION-LOG.md

# NOTE: `.github/` is deliberately NOT ignored any more.
#
# It was, back when releases here were hand-uploaded to a separate repo — the
# workflow fires on every `v*` tag and publishes its own release with that tag,
# which collided with a hand-built one. On the shared Asaw2011/nimbus repo that
# workflow IS the release mechanism: it builds macOS (arm64 + Intel), Windows
# and Linux and publishes all four installers, which is why that repo's releases
# have .dmg and .AppImage assets a Windows-only local build cannot produce.
#
# ⚠ Ignoring it meant a push from here would have DELETED it from his repo and
# silently broken cross-platform releases. Leave it tracked. Tag a release
# rather than hand-uploading, and let the workflow build it.
